# __PROJECT_NAME__-main

Project hub for **__PROJECT_NAME__**. A small meta-repo that holds:

- `project.yaml` — registry of all sub-repos
- `AGENTS.md` — project map for AI-assisted work (canonical, agent-neutral)
- `CLAUDE.md` — thin `@AGENTS.md` import (Claude Code compatibility)
- `invoke-ai.sh` — agent picker launcher (claude, omp, …) run across the sub-repos
- `.claude/skills/` — vendored conventions (works without the marketplace plugin)

The actual code lives in subfolders, each its own git repo. The hub's `.gitignore` keeps them out of this repo's history.

## Quick start

```bash
# Clone all registered sub-repos (skips ones you don't have access to)
# Run from a /ws-hub repos clone command inside claude, or manually:
#   git clone <url> ./<name>   for each in project.yaml

# Pick an agent (claude / omp) and launch across all available sub-repos
./invoke-ai.sh
```

## Layout

```
__PROJECT_NAME__-main/
├── project.yaml         # repo registry
├── AGENTS.md            # AI project map (canonical, agent-neutral)
├── CLAUDE.md            # thin @AGENTS.md import
├── invoke-ai.sh         # launcher (agent picker)
├── README.md
├── .gitignore           # managed block ignores sub-repo subfolders
├── .claude/skills/      # vendored conventions
├── __PROJECT_NAME__-app/        # own git, gitignored
├── __PROJECT_NAME__-marketing/  # own git, gitignored
└── ...
```

## Managing the hub

Use the `ws` plugin hub verbs: `/ws-hub repos <pull|clone>`, `/ws-hub status`, `/ws-hub add [--scan]`, `/ws-hub describe`.
